{
 "question": "What do the metadata containers of a stream of the AC-3 family declare of themselves, what does the sequence counter of its JOC payloads do, and what is either worth as a rule?",
 "method": "A container declares the version of its syntax, a key identifier and the lengths of two protection words (ETSI TS 102 366 clauses H.2.2.2.2, H.2.2.2.3, H.2.2.4.1 and H.2.2.4.2); the JOC payload of a frame carries a sequence counter (ETSI TS 103 420 clause 6.3.3.3). `verify` counts both and files five rules, all at `info`. The words themselves are keyed, their computation is not public, and nothing here reads one: what is counted is what is declared. `tools/rule_census.py` ran `verify --json` over the streams of the corpus; `tools/sweep.py` ran it over the first minute of every AC-3 and E-AC-3 track of a library. The streams are media and are not in the repository.",
