 "reading": "Every stream declares one thing from its first container to its last: over 79598 containers of the corpus and 688011 of the library not one names another key identifier or another length of a word than the container before it, none codes the reserved length, and none is of another syntax version. Two key identifiers are in use, 0 and 1, and a stream has one of them. The sequence counter starts again in 3 of 1260 tracks of the library (128 of them with JOC), and where it does it is no splice: each of those tracks holds the counter at 0 over its first frames (31, 47, 375 of them) and counts on from there, in one run. The one stream of the corpus that restarts is the head of the one that holds it longest, kept for it. A counter that does not follow was found in 0 tracks. So the five stay at `info`: three have never fired on a real stream and would mark one that changed hands, one fires on streams that are sound, and one has yet to be seen. A minute of a track is its head; what a whole track does at a seamless branch or a reel change is not in this count."
}
